// result_end
\caption(The only triangle remains present as its apex height shrinks to one millionth, correcting the reproduced missing-face case. Measured angles coincide with the analytic prediction and tend towards zero on logarithmic axes.)
\alttext(Native minimum-angle values and atan predictions coincide along an almost straight increasing line on log-log coordinates. As apex height decreases, the minimum angle approaches zero despite exact Delaunay topology.)

The new incircle predicate expands the four-row determinant into 48 signed
products of four decoded dyadic coordinates. Each product has at most 212
mantissa bits and a bounded exponent offset. In units of 2^−4296, the full
sum needs at most 8,398 bits; each signed-magnitude accumulator provides
8,448 bits. Consequently no fixed-integer carry escapes, even for subnormal
or largest-finite inputs. This is an exact sign for the supplied binary64
values, without tolerances, floating products or assumptions about
long-double width. It is a different implementation from Shewchuk's adaptive
floating expansions, while addressing the same determinant-sign problem.
The orientation predicate already uses the corresponding bounded-dyadic
method. Approximate minimum-angle calculations are separately scaled to
avoid overflow and may return zero after extreme relative-scale loss;
these diagnostics never decide the mesh topology.

Cocircular sites allow several Delaunay triangulations. The uncomplicated
straight-line Voronoi dual interpretation is clearest in general position;
with degeneracy, several circumcentres can coincide and the dual Delaunay
cell need not itself be triangular. The existing Voronoi API's finite/unbounded
cell conventions are unchanged. This report does not implement constrained
boundaries, holes, Steiner refinement or quality meshing.

> Actual quadratic conflict scans and complete limits

After k distinct noncollinear sites have been inserted, the finite faces
number 2k−2−h and ghosts number h, leaving exactly 2k−2 live faces. Full
scanning before each of the u−3 later insertions therefore performs

\[
\sum_{k=3}^{u-1}(2k-2)=u(u-3)
\]
\alttext(Summing the live finite-plus-ghost face count from three inserted sites to u minus one gives u times u minus three conflict tests.)

This count includes finite incircle and ghost half-plane calls. It excludes
seed selection, new-face orientation checks, edge maps, trace copying and
predicate-internal arithmetic. With ordered duplicate/cavity maps and full
live scans, the implementation has the conservative worst-case bound
O(n log(n+1)+u² log(u+1)), rather than a claim of a fast O(n log n)
triangulator. The active mesh, working cavities and identity maps use O(n+u)
storage. Complete trace events can add O(u²) storage over a whole run.
The exact conflict count is a work invariant, not an elapsed-time benchmark.

The trace checks the complete original-record cap before allocation, the
prospective full-scan cumulative conflict cap before each scan, and the
retained event-entry cap before retaining an insertion. One event entry is
charged for the insertion plus each removed face, boundary edge and added
face, including ghosts. Temporary cavities, input/maps and final output are
not included in that history count. Analysis separately caps every prospective
face/nonvertex-site circle query. Zero disables only an optional cap, while
arithmetic/capacity checks remain. Failures return no partial triangulation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/delaunay_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> size,actual,predicted,square;
  std::print("| distinct sites u | finite faces | hull boundary h | finite circle tests | ghost side tests | total conflict tests | u(u-3) |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{8,16,32,64,128}) {
    const auto t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(dm::geometry::delaunay_uniform_cloud(n,1981));const auto a=dm::geometry::delaunay_analyze(t.points,t.triangles);const auto tests=t.work.incircle_tests+t.work.hull_side_tests;
    if(a.used_points!=n || a.interior_violations || a.triangles!=2*n-2-a.boundary_edges || tests!=n*(n-3))return 1;
    size.push_back(n);actual.push_back(tests);predicted.push_back(n*(n-3));square.push_back(n*n);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,a.triangles,a.boundary_edges,t.work.incircle_tests,t.work.hull_side_tests,tests,n*(n-3));
  }
  const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> p{{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}};const auto t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p);std::size_t entries=0;for(const auto& e:t.steps)entries+=1+e.removed.size()+e.boundary.size()+e.added.size();int rejected=0;
  try{(void)dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p,4,10,entries);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p,5,9,entries);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p,5,10,entries-1);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::geometry::delaunay_analyze(p,t.triangles,7);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::geometry::delaunay_triangulation({{std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),0}});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  const auto exact=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p,5,10,entries),disabled=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace(p,0,0,0);
  const auto duplicated=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{1,0},{0,1},{0,0}}),line=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{1,0},{2,0}});
  if(rejected!=5 || exact.triangles.size()!=4 || disabled.triangles.size()!=4 || duplicated.representative_for_input.back()!=0 || line.has_seed)return 1;
  std::print("\nFive expected rejections: original-record cap, complete scan cap, event-entry cap, complete analysis cap, nonfinite short input. Count {}. Exact fan limits: records 5, conflicts 10, entries {}; all succeed, as do zero-disabled optional caps.\n",rejected,entries);
  std::print("Duplicate control: {} distinct sites, duplicate maps to original id {}, faces {}. Collinear control: has seed {}, faces {}.\n",duplicated.representatives.size(),duplicated.representative_for_input.back(),duplicated.triangles.size(),line.has_seed,line.triangles.size());
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(size,actual,"actual scans",{37,99,235},2).points(size,predicted,"u(u-3)",{31,41,55},4).line(size,square,"u squared",{220,38,38},2)
   .legend({"actual scans","u(u-3)","u squared"},{{37,99,235},{31,41,55},{220,38,38}})
   .title("Full live-face scans follow the exact quadratic law u(u-3)")
   .x_label("distinct noncollinear sites u").y_label("finite plus ghost conflict tests")
   .x_limits(0,140).y_limits(0,20500).size(1100,580).save_svg("build/delaunay_work.svg");
}
